rem Music festival
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=475

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg N integer = 600

rem Inclusion-exclusion over pairs of
rem one quartet in one trio: such a
rem pair set glues a quartet into
rem blocks, sizes 1+1+1+1, 2+1+1 (6
rem ways, sign -1), 2+2 (3, +1) or 3+1
rem (4, weight 2), i.e. A^4 - 6 A^2 B
rem + 3 B^2 + 8 A C. With a singles,
rem b pairs and c triples, the trios
rem form in a! / (6^q q!), q = (a -
rem b) / 3 trios of three singles.
Md = 1000000007
M = N // 4
Fc = (1 to 4 * M) scan * with 1
Fc = Fc mod Md
Fi = Fc (Md - 2) Md powmod
rem All i + j + k + l = M quartets of
rem the four kinds.
M1 = M + 1
Ix = (0 till M1 ** 3) copy
I = Ix // (M1 * M1)
J = Ix // M1 mod M1
K = Ix mod M1
L = M - I - J - K
Ok = L at least 0
A = 4 * I + 2 * J + L
B = J + 2 * K
Ok = Ok and (A at least B)
Ks = Ok indices
I = I Ks
J = J Ks
K = K Ks
L = L Ks
A = A Ks
Q = (A - B Ks) // 3
rem Multinomial, signs and weights.
Tm = (Fc M) * (Fi I) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (Fi J) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (Fi K) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (Fi L) mod Md
Tm = Tm * ((Md - 6) J Md powmod) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (3 K Md powmod) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (8 L Md powmod) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (Fc A) mod Md
I6 = 6 (Md - 2) Md powmod
Tm = Tm * (I6 Q Md powmod) mod Md
Tm = Tm * (Fi Q) mod Md
Answer = Tm sum mod Md
Answer print
